(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Writing Mathematics in Notebooks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"2ef29507-d11f-44a7-ab92-ea3a102fa645"],

Cell["MathNotebook Tutorial", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"35a5524b-a898-4f94-9b4c-9ad60460f071"],

Cell["\<\
How to write a mathematics paper in a Wolfram notebook: journal stylesheets, \
live referencing, and conversion between LaTeX source and native typeset \
math. Whether the mathematics is written as LaTeX or as built-in typeset math \
is your choice throughout \[LongDash] the palette only moves a selection from \
one to the other.\
\>", "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"d3598ab0-d926-4ddb-8638-63173f67edd3"],

Cell["Getting Started", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"95923a0c-00be-4ff2-b585-38127edc7491"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "After installing the paclet, restart the front end so that ",
 StyleBox["Palettes \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the stylesheet menu appear."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a0fa314c-ff0d-45b5-98b0-3845afeeeb95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Apply a stylesheet first \[LongDash] this is the step to do before anything \
else. ",
 StyleBox["Document view \[RightArrow] Apply stylesheet \[RightArrow] \
PlainArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " on the palette, or ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Stylesheet \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in that menu takes it back."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b0700f48-aacd-4a07-aff4-fdd5873ea417"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is not optional. The twelve block environments are ",
 StyleBox["declared by the stylesheet",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", so on a notebook still using ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " a Definition cell gets no name, no number and no indent, and a \
cross-reference to it renders ",
 StyleBox["2.0",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the section counter increments and the theorem counter never \
does. That reads as a broken paclet and is a missing step."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cc74901a-df18-47b2-9c4e-7b7908c8d197"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PlainArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is the one to start from: the notebook\[CloseCurlyQuote]s own typography \
with the paper structure added. The five journal templates below are for a \
submission, and an imported ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " picks its own sheet from its ",
 StyleBox["\\documentclass",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"376dd13c-38e5-4165-9704-e86733d42bf5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Then ",
 StyleBox["Blocks \[RightArrow] Front matter",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " puts empty ",
 StyleBox["Title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cells at the top of the document and leaves the cursor in the title \
\[LongDash] in that order, which is the order ",
 StyleBox["\\maketitle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " needs them in. It is one of only two buttons that ignore the selection, \
the other being ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Write the body in ",
 StyleBox["Section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c25163bd-fb06-4b6f-9b9b-d6401e9ff410"],

Cell["\<\
Every palette button acts on the notebook you were last editing, and on its \
current selection.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5c1b8f47-c600-44da-98e9-9cf098a079a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The journal stylesheets are light-only; applying one from the palette\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 StyleBox["Document view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group also sets the notebook to light mode, so printed and exported output \
matches the screen. Applying a sheet clears the two size overrides below it, \
the new sheet replacing them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"61113f89-3e2e-475d-93b7-2619f52de119"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Update from cloud",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", in the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Setup",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group, asks the Wolfram Cloud which version is published and installs it \
only when it is newer than the one you have \[LongDash] so checking costs a \
line of text, not a download. It then rebuilds the front end menus and \
reopens the palette, which makes the new palette, stylesheets and tutorial \
live immediately."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"acbaaaed-b760-4969-babf-0cb3ddd3df18"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It always says which of three things happened: updated, with the old and \
new version numbers; already current; or the cloud could not be reached. \
Kernel code from the new version loads after ",
 StyleBox["Evaluation \[RightArrow] Quit Kernel",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the button will not quit the kernel out from under your \
session."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"77db8278-8668-42d9-8aa1-beac298a46e2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A copy loaded from a development directory shadows anything installed from \
the cloud, so the button reports that and downloads nothing. The same check \
from code: ",
 StyleBox["UpdateMathNotebook[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d86f96d7-86e6-4392-a086-57b618611c00"],

Cell["Referencing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0e33b3e3-d4d9-4977-a97f-c6fdea20e5f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select a numbered cell \[LongDash] an equation, a theorem, a section, a \
numbered item \[LongDash] and press ",
 StyleBox["Copy reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then paste into your text."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a3fe86db-3dcf-4fa5-9510-4859e543dcf1"],

Cell["\<\
The pasted reference is a live button showing the current number, so \
reordering cells renumbers every reference to them.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d6b13c6e-b8fc-4dee-838e-c30df0bff39d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Clicking a reference jumps to its target; ",
 StyleBox["\[UpArrow] Go back",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns to where you clicked from."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e47cfafe-8207-495c-8709-642bf14661a7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", in the ",
 StyleBox["Blocks",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group, adds a bibliography entry: it asks for a citation key and puts a \
tagged, labelled entry at the end of the bibliography \[LongDash] starting \
one, under a ",
 StyleBox["References",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " heading, if the notebook has none yet. It goes there rather than at the \
cursor, unlike every other button in that group."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"15a6f401-b8ab-4500-b4cf-ca809ca5d68b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Insert citation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " then offers everything the notebook has tagged, literature entries and \
numbered blocks in two lists, with a filter field; picking one inserts a red \
bracketed link to it. Type a key the notebook does not have and it cites that \
instead, so a citation can be written before its target exists. To name a \
cell yourself, use ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Cell Tags",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"95c1953a-d7f8-46d0-9596-5d3a384d7d67"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A citation to a numbered environment shows its number instead of its tag: \
tag a theorem, cite it, and the citation reads ",
 StyleBox["Theorem 1.1",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] renumbering itself when cells move, in the exported PDF as on \
screen. A tag no cell carries yet keeps its brackets, so a citation written \
before its target is still readable."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"86099d0e-6243-4b40-a3d6-23a29e31b396"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tagging a ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell also labels it: the entry shows its tag in brackets in the margin, \
which is exactly what a citation to it reads, so the bibliography and the \
body agree without your typing either."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cd1a056e-26cf-4bfe-92cf-f51a08098d07"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Cell Tags dialog sets the tag and not the label, so after tagging an \
entry that way press ",
 StyleBox["Refresh labels",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] it labels every entry of the notebook at once, and clears the \
label of an entry whose tag you removed. From code, ",
 StyleBox["LabelReferences[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5ee593c6-c4f0-48cc-b970-a9ee50910b94"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Sort bibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reorders the entries: by first citation, which is what BibTeX\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s unsrt prints, by key, or by the entry text. ",
 StyleBox["Report uncited",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sorts nothing and answers the question a sort cannot \[LongDash] which \
entries nothing cites, and which citations point at no cell. Where the \
entries came from a ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", the order shown is the notebook\[CloseCurlyQuote]s alone: that file and \
its style decide what the compiled paper prints."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cf916179-92a1-4f98-ac4b-63736c876947"],

Cell["\<\
The theorem below and the equation after it are practice targets: select \
either one and copy a reference to it.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8121a15f-a6cb-401f-a64d-dc7bf59f5fcf"],

Cell["The exponential map is surjective onto the unit circle.", "Theorem",ExpressionUUID->"c51ec6de-dc6c-42d6-8575-f8df72ed8f8a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", "\[Pi]"}]], "+", "1", "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"f98e3c49-bb74-\
4b0c-82fd-9f1caf715632"],

Cell["Stylesheets", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"97facf9c-b233-45dc-8cd6-bcb18cbdcf1a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Five templates: ",
 StyleBox["AMSArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (amsart, Palatino), ",
 StyleBox["ArXivArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (article, Latin Modern), ",
 StyleBox["SpringerJournal",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["RevTeXAPS",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (Times), and ",
 StyleBox["ComplexSystems",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", which is the journal's own page rather than a resemblance of one: a 306 \
pt column on a 432 \[Times] 648 sheet, with display mathematics flush left."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"92b4c480-5156-4d00-ba23-a2ff1c9b5f15"],

Cell["\<\
All five define the same style names, so switching between them is instant \
and changes nothing but the typography.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d24fd7fe-3576-42ab-b724-fd294a771b0b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PlainArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a fifth sheet and not a template: it is the notebook's own typography \
with the paper structure added, and it is what an imported paper opens on \
when its \\documentclass names no journal above."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"aa03caa2-b194-4c4e-9c24-6e4862ce28e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Theorem, Lemma, Proposition, Corollary, Conjecture, Claim, Definition, \
Example, Construction, Remark, Question, and Observation share a single \
counter that resets at each section, exactly as in LaTeX; numbered equations \
count continuously through the document. ",
 StyleBox["ComplexSystems",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is the exception its journal makes: there each of the twelve counts on its \
own, with no section number in front of it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"befab088-db9b-456f-b9b5-4a0816ca6141"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Insert environments from the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Insert environment",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu, or with the ",
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["Equation (n)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " buttons."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c159cf57-3e3c-4de9-adc7-479dc7e5cae4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A block is not confined to one cell. Put an equation inside a definition \
and press ",
 StyleBox["Continue block",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to carry the prose on: the new cell repeats the block's own style, showing \
no second name and taking no second number, so it lines up with the prose \
above it instead of at the plain text margin 64 pt to its left. A ",
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " carried on this way keeps its QED square at the end, where it belongs."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fa57395f-b5ea-44ea-bd22-0e40ff2ef606"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern and TeX Gyre are LaTeX fonts, not system fonts: press ",
 StyleBox["Install LaTeX fonts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " once to copy them out of a local TeX distribution (",
 ButtonBox["tug.org/texlive",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 ") into your user font directory, then restart the front end. They are \
installed for the whole machine, not inside Mathematica, so any application \
can use them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b6cf5233-78e5-4d87-a188-e114ad1661ff"],

Cell["Reading and Writing Comfortably", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3c105933-11b2-4452-8862-892b0c9aa722"],

Cell["\<\
Each palette group folds: click its opener or its name to collapse it, so \
only the buttons you are using take up room. The palette remembers which \
groups are open across front end restarts.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2766f636-3828-4f4c-b983-d18b76664935"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Document view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group holds two sliders and a reset. Like every other palette control they \
act on the notebook you were last editing, so leave the palette open beside \
your paper and drag while you read it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"189d8e7c-8bd4-46d8-89f5-7e052c893e16"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Text size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sets the size of ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and scales the whole document with it \[LongDash] the title, the headings, \
the abstract, the theorem environments, proofs, bibliography entries, both \
kinds of list, and the mathematics: displayed equations, their numbers, \
inline mathematics and MaTeX cells alike \[LongDash] so the page keeps its \
proportions instead of one style growing alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1b59dfa4-d6b7-401a-8d7f-04b9bf2c08e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sizes the mathematics on its own, and only if you touch it. Leave it where \
it is and mathematics follows ",
 StyleBox["Text size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; set it and it overrides that, which is what to reach for when a journal's \
equations want to be larger or smaller than the sheet makes them relative to \
the prose."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"777ef1a9-7571-4075-8b25-73552cf5d643"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both set real font sizes, so they reach the exported PDF. ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Magnification",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a different thing entirely \[LongDash] it zooms the screen and never \
changes print."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cbe16d11-46d9-4a00-8e66-37fa6ca2ea7d"],

Cell["\<\
The settings are stored in the notebook itself, so they survive saving and \
reopening and travel with the file to a coauthor.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7fc03c02-8743-420b-b49e-76a042c4bc2d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reset view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns the notebook to its stylesheet\[CloseCurlyQuote]s own sizes; \
applying a stylesheet clears the overrides too, since the new sheet replaces \
them. The document keeps a private stylesheet of its own afterwards, which \
changes nothing you can see \[LongDash] every style is written at the sheet\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s own size \[LongDash] but does mean ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Stylesheet",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " no longer shows the sheet ticked. That is deliberate: assigning a \
stylesheet by name onto a document that carries size overrides can leave the \
front end unable to print, so the paclet never does it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bf3c7aa2-1273-4ced-a0d7-b3cf33d1bf29"],

Cell["\<\
MaTeX cells are images and cannot inherit a style, so either slider \
re-renders each of them through LaTeX at the new size, from the TeX the cell \
stores.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4a121d58-5845-4a71-aa17-6f935d8bc04a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["SetDocumentFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["SetMathFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] each takes ",
 StyleBox["Automatic",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop its own override \[LongDash] and ",
 StyleBox["ResetDocumentView[nb]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop all of them. They work on a notebook still using ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " too."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e56a79bd-1a63-4de6-8919-eac06cc81df9"],

Cell["Math Input Shortcuts", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a1fdec6f-2df9-4484-a176-eb3c6fbcdade"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " inline math in text, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " exits."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"02d07d7c-ff68-43fc-9618-6d325b1f22e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+/",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fraction, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " square root."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a6c5e9f3-da1b-484f-b61d-680679f91c16"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+^",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " superscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+_",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " subscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " switches between them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7584d0e2-2904-4ef1-a19f-d43bf4aa464b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["name",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " enters symbols: ",
 StyleBox["a",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Alpha], ",
 StyleBox["el",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Element], ",
 StyleBox["->",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Rule]."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6eb1f8de-62bd-45d0-a694-e7d09bf59fa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " shows the cell expression (",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on Windows)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3b5013dd-8f1b-4516-8765-4fa87e08bb88"],

Cell["Working with Cells", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3555ebe2-2c7e-47f6-b222-baa6dc4cb50e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Click a cell bracket to select the cell; drag across brackets to select \
several; ",
 StyleBox["Delete",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " removes them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3153ce10-8e33-47f8-bda9-5d3e821d02cf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " extends the selection outward; repeat to reach the whole cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"67e3440a-c72c-4461-92cc-5c255e66a217"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["7",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " restyle a cell: Title, Section, Subsection, Text, Input."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e70b34e4-d7e7-47a4-8998-ed43ef6f3086"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on a fresh cell inserts an ",
 StyleBox["Input",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell \[LongDash] the one to reach for when you replace an imported \
figure's ",
 StyleBox["Import",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " with the code that draws it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bea46ed7-b4be-4ed3-b35a-5bc7b0956b2d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+D",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " divides a cell at the cursor; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+M",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " merges selected cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bb5fc84e-9819-434c-9392-3f845ff8511d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " groups selected cells; ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ungroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"98051c48-952e-4e33-9a68-343dbe696147"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Double-click a group bracket to close or open the group; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+{",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+}",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " open and close all subgroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"66802b70-6577-4af6-8887-900b2580ce24"],

Cell["\<\
Double-click a closed group's remaining bracket to reopen it; use Cell \
\[RightArrow] Delete All Output before sharing a notebook.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"00c88703-e1ec-4d3e-a376-0af6ec091cff"],

Cell["LaTeX Conversion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"43baf1fc-5973-4da2-a0ae-6ebb7fa2c6cf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Import & Export",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group is the route for a paper; the ",
 StyleBox["Selection",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group acts on the cells you have selected. Hover any button for a sentence \
on what it does."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4dd36891-b8b6-4d8c-b8ff-18bf7fab83ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Import .tex file\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reads a whole paper into a new notebook: ",
 StyleBox["\\section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the theorem-like environments the preamble declares become cells of \
the matching style, mathematics is typeset, ",
 StyleBox["\\label",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes a cell tag, and ",
 StyleBox["\\ref",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\cite",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become live links. Anything it does not convert is carried verbatim, so \
what it cannot read it also does not damage."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"38cb8746-b712-49e9-b55f-cb18803d35cb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The front matter comes with it: ",
 StyleBox["\\title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\date",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become Title, Author and Date cells you can edit \[LongDash] the edit \
reaches the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] and an ",
 StyleBox["abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes Abstract cells, headed once however many paragraphs it runs to. ",
 StyleBox["\\maketitle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " has no content of its own, so it stays as text beside ",
 StyleBox["\\sloppy",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\tableofcontents",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4b0fb253-6861-453a-8963-ca921af20344"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["itemize",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["enumerate",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["description",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become Item and ItemNumbered cells, one per ",
 StyleBox["\\item",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", nesting into Subitem and Subsubitem. Each list restarts its numbering as \
LaTeX does, an ",
 StyleBox["\\item[label]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " prints the label instead of the number, and a second paragraph of one item \
becomes an ItemParagraph cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"de84e450-2019-49eb-9208-f9f08bca21e4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["figure",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes its caption plus an ",
 StyleBox["Input",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell holding the code that draws the picture \[LongDash] an ",
 StyleBox["Import",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of the file the paper shipped, which you replace with the Wolfram code \
that generates it. Evaluate the cell and the figure is live; the picture's \
own markup, TikZ included, still goes back into the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " untouched, so the generating code stays the notebook's alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"55700600-8aa3-4d14-80be-d28eae18be04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bibliography comes in whichever way the paper writes it. A ",
 StyleBox["thebibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes one Reference cell per ",
 StyleBox["\\bibitem",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", each showing its key in brackets exactly as the citations to it read, and \
each is yours to edit \[LongDash] the edit reaches the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Entries pulled from a ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become the same cells, but there the ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " stays the source of truth: only the ",
 StyleBox["\\bibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands go back out, so edit the ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and re-import. A declared ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that is not beside the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is reported rather than passed over in silence."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ce5a5fa2-de9a-46ef-b882-3f93a1b9fb39"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Export to .tex\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " writes the whole notebook back out as a paper. An imported one comes back \
as the source it was read from, edits and all; a notebook you wrote here \
comes out as LaTeX built from its styles. A block you typed goes out as a \
real environment, its continuation cells included \[LongDash] one ",
 StyleBox["\\begin{definition}",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and one ",
 StyleBox["\\end{definition}",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " around the whole of it \[LongDash] and in an imported paper under the name \
that paper's preamble declares. This is the export route \[LongDash] the two \
buttons below are for a handful of cells, not for a submission."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"237bb976-235f-4a64-a4dc-f8eb825de8a7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Export submission\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " writes the paper into a directory instead of into a file, and puts \
everything it needs to compile beside it: each figure file the ",
 StyleBox["\\includegraphics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands name, each ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " the preamble declares, and \[LongDash] where a local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is found \[LongDash] the ",
 StyleBox[".bbl",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", which arXiv needs because it runs LaTeX but does not run BibTeX. That \
directory is the upload. A ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " on its own names files that stayed behind and compiles nowhere but the \
paper's original directory, which is the whole reason this button exists \
beside the one above."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c822472e-218e-4a07-a72b-a5d82e27e74d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nothing arXiv rejects goes into it: no ",
 StyleBox[".aux",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox[".log",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and no compiled PDF \[LongDash] the LaTeX run happens in a scratch copy \
and only the ",
 StyleBox[".bbl",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " comes back. A file the paper names that is not on disk is reported by \
name, never quietly left out and never re-rendered from the notebook: the \
format and size the ",
 StyleBox["\\includegraphics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " assumes are not recoverable, and guessing them would be guessing at how \
you compile."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"dce4f62d-8c81-45dd-91a4-048bd9695e05"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Per-cell conversion has no button of its own \[LongDash] the whole-paper \
route above is the way out to LaTeX \[LongDash] but the two functions remain: \
",
 StyleBox["ConvertLaTeXCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reads the selected cells as LaTeX and replaces the mathematics in them \
with editable typeset math, and ",
 StyleBox["ConvertMathCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " turns it back into LaTeX you can read or paste elsewhere. With nothing \
selected, the whole notebook."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"261e193b-e6d0-4e84-8673-d9bdcb6dbef9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["ConvertLaTeXCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " parses inline ",
 StyleBox["$\[Ellipsis]$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\(\[Ellipsis]\\)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and displayed ",
 StyleBox["$$\[Ellipsis]$$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\[\[Ellipsis]\\]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; the starred forms stay unnumbered, the unstarred ones become numbered \
equations."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8576a3b1-b57c-4072-9082-e0c0c097ec7e"],

Cell["\<\
A display environment written inside a paragraph, with prose on the lines \
around it, is lifted out into its own equation cell and the prose stays in \
Text cells on either side.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ea850ca2-f931-41a2-a024-a0e9d5236669"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " environment becomes a grid aligned on its ",
 StyleBox["&",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", so it stays editable as one equation cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b92a506a-7237-4564-9cdd-b503094a8447"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each converted cell keeps its original TeX, so ",
 StyleBox["ConvertMathCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back what you typed rather than a re-serialization of the boxes. \
Anything the parser cannot read is left untouched."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"385d95ea-f5c4-4b8a-b4b9-893477ff54f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Input, Code, and Output cells are skipped, so ",
 StyleBox["$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in code is safe."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cc319504-93e0-415e-a78b-c423e9384f7f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["ImportLaTeXDocument[\"paper.tex\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["ExportLaTeXDocument[nb, \"paper.tex\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["ExportLaTeXBundle[nb, \"directory\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for the whole paper, ",
 StyleBox["ConvertLaTeXCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["ConvertMathCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for a selection."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7c56ae21-a668-46ee-84cb-7f0c692cd412"],

Cell["MaTeX", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5c0f32ca-0978-451b-a87f-3c5bd3a7b718"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX (",
 ButtonBox["github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"],
 ") is optional, and needs a TeX distribution and Ghostscript. It is used \
only by the two ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " buttons in the ",
 StyleBox["Selection",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group; referencing, stylesheets, and LaTeX conversion do not."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"86207046-592c-46c9-a914-42afcfd1144f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use it when an equation has to come out of real LaTeX \[LongDash] macros, \
",
 StyleBox["tikz-cd",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " diagrams, exact journal metrics."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"826d13b8-63c4-4330-99a5-c3e81d1ea985"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Install MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " installs the paclet and points it at the local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["gs",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0f0627bd-a748-4fff-938a-fbeac6825f38"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["math \[Rule] MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sends the selected display equations through LaTeX, at whatever size ",
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is showing mathematics at; ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back editable typeset math from the TeX stored in each cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"03467c64-3cc6-413b-8572-3337f9fa3a26"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MaTeX preferences",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " opens your ",
 StyleBox["init.m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in the front end \[LongDash] deliberately not through the system handler \
for ",
 StyleBox[".m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " files. Set the preamble, the magnification, and ",
 StyleBox["$useMaTeXQ = True",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to route TeX typed into a notebook through LaTeX instead of the built-in \
parser."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9408fac0-df7c-414d-8a6d-7640c7b72ffc"],

Cell["\<\
MaTeX cells are images: convert them back before editing, and keep rendering \
for last.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"85699027-c885-4178-92b0-7c6c61c97dc8"],

Cell["Best Practices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2c5b67e9-b11e-4ca6-9490-90b5aa061ab3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Insert blocks from the palette rather than restyling cells by hand, and \
carry one across cells with ",
 StyleBox["Continue block",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " rather than with a Text cell: the styles and counters stay consistent, and \
the whole block exports as one environment instead of the tail of it leaking \
out as bare prose."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ab92315b-98f2-41df-bb21-dfc310625541"],

Cell["\<\
Tag cells as you write them; tagging a theorem after fifty pages means \
finding it again.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"26246a87-d2e0-4912-bba1-8367465c4544"],

Cell["\<\
Do not strip cell tagging rules: they hold the TeX source that makes the \
round trip lossless.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8faa3452-1c7e-4d35-8060-32622695e26f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Export to .tex\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " at submission time, not continuously \[LongDash] the notebook is the \
source. Use ",
 StyleBox["Export submission\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " when the destination is arXiv: a ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " alone is not a submission."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"edb272cc-2314-4e12-a670-5b838ec343f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before sharing: ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Delete All Output",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " the MaTeX cells so a coauthor can edit them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7f17371b-1daa-4217-ade0-7ebb51c783f9"],

Cell["Credits", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a20a44d2-91ba-4a95-91d5-a3a14ad23808"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The referencing scheme and the MaTeX integration are originally due to Nik \
Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"],
 "; this paclet packages and extends that work."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f133c7f0-79ac-4a86-8d63-c1de606980d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nik Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[murzin]"]],
 ParagraphIndent->0,
 CellTags->"murzin",ExpressionUUID->"51442b28-7062-4634-80a5-1284f7d3e177"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Szabolcs Horvat, MaTeX: LaTeX labels in Mathematica, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[matex]"]],
 ParagraphIndent->0,
 CellTags->"matex",ExpressionUUID->"ac3c6aa8-46a2-4771-90be-0417a8c02523"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "TeX Live, ",
 ButtonBox["https://tug.org/texlive/",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 " \[LongDash] on macOS, MacTeX, ",
 ButtonBox["https://tug.org/mactex/",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/mactex/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/mactex/"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[texlive]"]],
 ParagraphIndent->0,
 CellTags->"texlive",ExpressionUUID->"fef389f4-a700-4cd0-afb1-f201f8c1be52"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern, ",
 ButtonBox["https://ctan.org/pkg/lm",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://ctan.org/pkg/lm"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://ctan.org/pkg/lm"],
 " and TeX Gyre, ",
 ButtonBox["https://ctan.org/pkg/tex-gyre",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://ctan.org/pkg/tex-gyre"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://ctan.org/pkg/tex-gyre"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[lm]"]],
 ParagraphIndent->0,
 CellTags->"lm",ExpressionUUID->"48123c61-a1ac-469c-82a7-97b068535d6e"]
},
LightDark->"Light",
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (May 19, 2026)",
